2026-08-08 Chronic Engineering — AQEMU 1.3.0 (Apple SoC Inferno + Reims WSL)

	* Version bump to 1.3.0 across code, MSI/MSIX, WiX, and packaging docs.
	* Apple SoC / iOS (ChefKiss Inferno):
	  - Inferno launch profile: trustcache, ticket, SEP FW/ROM, usb-conn, kaslr-off,
	    multi-ns NVMe + apple-nvram + SEP pflash image set under the VM folder.
	  - MACHINE tab owns all Inferno file paths (kernel, DeviceTree, trustcache,
	    ticket, SEP FW/ROM, optional SecureROM, IPSW) and USB remote / kaslr-off.
	    Launch never invents missing paths or injects default -append; Start validates
	    required MACHINE-tab fields and fails with a clear message instead.
	  - On Windows, applesoc is forced through WSL Linux qemu-system-applesoc
	    (UNIX sockets / companion restore; not Windows PE alone).
	  - File → Apple SoC Restore: companion helper; one-click SSH upload of IPSW
	    + idevicerestore inside the companion (sshpass via WSL).
	  - File → Apply iOS filesystem patches… (also MACHINE tab + Restore dialog +
	    post-restore prompt): InfernoFSPatcher + LaunchDaemons on the guest root
	    NVMe via WSL KVM helper — not the companion. Required for SpringBoard;
	    clears Restore ramdisk (-initrd) on success. Bundles extras/Inferno scripts.
	  - Session toolbar (Apple SoC): Home / Side / Vol / SOS / More… / Pad / Net via
	    Inferno F-key sendkey; floating pad is neutral (not an iPhone bezel).
	  - File / VM → Guest Internet / iOS Device Tools… (toolbar Net): Enable guest
	    internet (reverse-tether) on the companion — usbmuxd MODE=3 + NetworkManager
	    Shared on USB/NCM (not the AQEMU Network NIC tab). Marks Ubuntu ethernet
	    managed so Shared activation is not “strictly unmanaged”. Diagnose USB /
	    idevice; IPA install via ideviceinstaller (auto-apt if missing); screenshot.
	  - extras/Inferno/iOS_Installation.md: starter + re-install walkthrough
	    (restore, FS patches, internet, IPA vs .deb, 8 GiB vs 32 GiB root).
	    File → iOS Firmware Tool forges restore/SEP tickets and packs SEP firmware
	    in-app (bundled create_*ticket.py; img4 / pyimg4). File → Configure sets
	    Python / pyimg4 / img4 paths (PATH fallback if empty).
	    wipe-ios-nvme.ps1 for partial-flash / clean NAND. Default auto-created root
	    is 8 GiB; grow sparse to 32 GiB before restore for App Store / large IPAs.
	    FS-patch helper selects the iOS NVMe by skipping the cloud-image boot disk
	    (works for 8 GiB and 32 GiB roots). Companion SSH uses accept-new + a
	    dedicated known_hosts file (loopback only).
	  - Restore ramdisk (-initrd) also sets boot-mode=enter_recovery so NVRAM
	    auto-boot=true cannot skip recovery on re-restore.
	  - Apple SoC QEMU stop: short summary first (full kernel-patch dump stays in
	    qemu-boot.log / Error Log); Copy on error dialogs is usable.
	  - Embedded VNC: sticky mouse grab no longer steals File/toolbar; leave and
	    chrome clicks release grab.
	  - Wizard + main UI fields for Inferno firmware paths and USB remote type.
	* Hardware-accelerated Intel macOS (Reims):
	  - Always uses Linux qemu-system-reims3d under WSL with reims-vgpu-pci.
	  - Documents AMD and NVIDIA host GPUs via WSLg Vulkan (not Windows PE Reims).
	  - Reims computer type locks Video Card to reims-vgpu-pci only (UI/wizard/args);
	    cirrus/std from the PE probe catalog are never offered or persisted.
	  - Product display: -display none + embedded VNC for OpenCore/early boot.
	    QEMU SDL/GTK (Separate QEMU window) is blocked for Reims on WSL (DRI3).
	    REIMS_VGPU_WINDOW defaults off: Mesa Dozen on WSLg NVIDIA can segfault in
	    vkCreateDevice and kill QEMU; opt-in under Advanced Settings → WSL.
	  - Wizard/start injects reims-vgpu-efi.efi into OpenCore and prefers OVMF_CODE_4M.
	* WSL: prompt for distro/username on boot when missing; optional password can be
	  saved securely in Windows Credential Manager (never AQEMU.ini). KVM access
	  prefers wsl -u root, with sudo -S stdin fallback when Remember is enabled.
	  Reims VM provision/start auto-installs native-arch Mesa Dozen (dzn)
	  Vulkan-on-D3D12 ICD in WSL (ignores foreign multiarch dzn; strips
	  conflicting mesa-vulkan-drivers:<foreign-arch>). Treats native
	  libvulkan_dzn as ready even when vulkaninfo segfaults/lists nothing.
	  Probe Dozen via wsl -e (not wsl --) so login-shell $(…) expansion cannot
	  falsely report the ICD missing. Reims attach uses pci-bridge +
	  reims-vgpu-gop.rom (UEFI GOP); Intel/Reims prefer OSX-KVM OVMF_CODE_4M
	  over stock edk2 when available. Machine -machine path props rewritten for WSL.

2026-07-31 Chronic Engineering — AQEMU 1.0.2 (Reims vGPU Acceleration Target)

	* Virtual GPU Acceleration Target (qemu-system-reimsvgpu.exe):
	  - Built and bundled steelbrain qemu-reims-vgpu engine into AQEMU as a standalone executable.
	  - Enabled libslirp User-Mode NAT networking, SPICE display streaming, and DirectSound audio.
	* New VM Wizard & OS Integration:
	  - Added "macOS x86_64 vGPU (Reims)" under Apple operating systems tree.
	  - Added "Windows 11 vGPU (Reims)" under Windows operating systems tree.
	  - Registered "x86_64 vGPU (Reims)" -> qemu-system-reimsvgpu in Architecture Targets.
	  - Configured 8GB RAM, 4 vCPUs, and virtio vGPU display presets.
	* Probing & Catalog Automation:
	  - Registered qemu-system-reimsvgpu.exe in probe_qemu.py and generated reimsvgpu.json catalog.

2026-07-31 Chronic Engineering — AQEMU 1.0.1 (Apple Silicon / iOS Emulation & ChefKiss Inferno)

	* Apple Silicon (ARM64) SoC Emulation Target (qemu-system-applesoc.exe):
	  - Built and bundled ChefKiss Inferno (QEMU 10.0+ fork for Apple Silicon SoCs) into AQEMU.
	  - Linked liblzfse for LZFSE kernel cache decompression and Apple raw kernel cache booting.
	  - Integrated Nettle & GMP crypto libraries for Apple Secure Enclave Processor (SEP) emulation.
	  - Enabled libslirp User-Mode NAT networking and SPICE display/audio backends.
	* New VM Wizard Integration:
	  - Added "iOS (ARM64)" and "macOS Apple Silicon (ARM64)" to Apple OS selection tree.
	  - Mapped "iPhone 11 (Apple A13 Bionic)" -> t8030 machine and "iPhone 6s Plus (Apple A9)" -> s8000.
	  - Registered "Apple Silicon SoC" (qemu-system-applesoc) in Architecture Targets and probe script.
	  - Created automatic wizard presets with 4 vCPUs, 4GB RAM, virtio-net-pci, and NVMe APFS disk defaults.
	* Probing & Ground-Truth Catalog:
	  - Updated probe_qemu.py and qemu_probe_full_v3 dataset generator to register qemu-system-applesoc.exe.

2026-07-23 Chronic Engineering — AQEMU 1.0.0

	* Version bump to 1.0.0 — first public “curtain” release for community testing.
	* QEMU CLI parity waves: Advanced Options for NUMA, watchdog, TPM, secrets,
	  incoming migrate, SMBIOS, fw_cfg, audiodev, icount/sandbox, richer chardev.
	* Blockdev graph editor + migrate progress/cancel (QMP) UI.
	* VM-start UX: busy dialog, async QMP connect (no UI freeze).
	* Guest profile polish: Solaris 11.4 x86 recipe, AIX/pseries (no WHPX/floppy/IDE),
	  OS/2 / ReactOS / Win9x / XP proven defaults in the wizard.
	* Windows: pure TCG for non-x86 guests (ppc64 etc.); quoted Additional Args;
	  qemu-img VMDK size parse fix; quieter startup / clearer breadcrumbs.
	* README refreshed for testers; Windows portable zip = AQEMU + QEMU 11.0.2.

